\p{The solid curve is the voltage nullcline and the dashed line is
#{w=V/2}. The marked point is the origin. For #{a=0.1} one orbit
starts at #{(0.55,0)} and one at #{(-0.4,0.06)}. Both end at the
origin. For #{a=-0.1} one orbit starts at #{(0.18,0)} and moves to
the right, and one starts at #{(-0.15,0.16)} and moves to the left.
Each initial point is chosen for the drawing.}
